## Review Instructions

Examine the diff above. Classify every finding into one of two categories:

**Functional Issues** — will cause errors, crashes, or data loss if left unfixed:
  Bugs, crashes, null derefs, security vulnerabilities, data loss, injection, auth bypass

**Design Suggestions** — code works correctly but could be improved:
  Naming clarity, code duplication, performance optimization, testability, idiomatic patterns

Rules:
1. Every finding MUST include: file path + line number + relevant code snippet as evidence. Findings without code-level evidence will be rejected.
2. Before applying any edit (when edit mode is enabled), you MUST first Read the target file to confirm its current content. Do not rely on the diff alone.
3. Functional Issues and Design Suggestions must be reported in separate sections — never mix them in the same list.

